---
import Page from "../../layouts/Page.astro";
import TopBar from "../../components/TopBar.astro";
import { v, importmap } from "../../lib/v.mjs";
---
<Page
  title="Redirect Import: Spreadsheet to Redirect File | jsal.io"
  description="Turn a spreadsheet of old and new addresses into the redirect file Shopify, WordPress, Wix and others import, each one checked first. Free, nothing uploaded."
  path="/redirects/"
  ogTitle="Redirect Import: Spreadsheet to Redirect File | jsal.io"
  ogDescription="Turn a spreadsheet of old and new addresses into the redirect file your platform imports, with every address checked first. Free and entirely in your browser."
  ogImage="redirects"
  ogImageAlt="Redirect Import: a sheet of old and new addresses, checked and ready to import"
  icon="/img/icons/redirect-import.svg"
  mono={false}
>
<script is:inline slot="head" type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebApplication",
    "name": "Redirect Import",
    "url": "https://jsal.io/redirects/",
    "description": "Paste or drop a spreadsheet of old and new addresses and get the redirect import file for Shopify, WordPress (Redirection, Rank Math, Yoast), Wix, Squarespace, Webflow, Framer, HubSpot, BigCommerce, Duda, Ghost, Netlify, Vercel, Apache or Nginx. Checks every address first. Runs entirely in the browser.",
    "applicationCategory": "UtilitiesApplication",
    "operatingSystem": "Any (web browser)",
    "isAccessibleForFree": true,
    "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD" },
    "author": { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://jsal.io/#john", "name": "John Salvador", "url": "https://jsal.io/" },
    "isPartOf": { "@id": "https://jsal.io/#website" }
  }
  </script>
<link slot="head" rel="stylesheet" href={v("styles.css", "/redirects/")}>
<script is:inline slot="head" type="importmap" set:html={importmap("/redirects/", ["./js/main.js", "./js/core.js", "./js/formats.js", "./js/xlsx.js"])}></script>
<script is:inline slot="head" type="module" src={v("js/main.js", "/redirects/")}></script>
  <main class="app" id="app">

    <!-- Top bar shared by every jsal.io app (styles in /shell.css; the logo menu and theme button come from /nav.js) -->
    <TopBar class="app-header"><h1 slot="title" class="jsal-title"><img class="jsal-title-ico" src={v("/img/icons/redirect-import.svg")} alt="" width="22" height="22">Redirect <span class="hl">Import</span><span class="sr-only">: spreadsheet to redirect file</span></h1>
<a class="jsal-link" href="#about">About</a></TopBar>
    <p class="jsal-for">For web teams moving a site: turn a sheet of old and new addresses into the file Shopify, WordPress, Wix and others import.</p>

    <!-- Where the file goes, and what to do with it -->
    <div class="bar">
      <label class="plat"><span class="label">Import into</span><select class="field" id="platform"></select></label>
      <p class="where"><a id="whereDoc" href="https://jsal.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Help page</a></p>
      <p class="summary" id="summary" aria-live="polite" data-needs-content></p>
      <div class="bar-actions" data-needs-content>
        <button type="button" class="jsal-btn" id="copyBtn">Copy file</button>
        <button type="button" class="jsal-btn" id="downloadBtn">Download file</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="work" id="work" data-view="sheet">

      <!-- Empty state: paste anywhere on the page, drop a file, or start a sheet by hand -->
      <div class="drop" id="drop" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Add your redirects">
        <svg class="drop-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h11M11 3l4 4-4 4M20 17H9M13 13l-4 4 4 4"/></svg>
        <p class="drop-title">Paste or drop your redirects</p>
        <p class="drop-sub" data-touch="Copy the old and new address columns from Excel or Google Sheets and tap Paste, or choose a CSV or Excel file.">Copy the old and new address columns from Excel or Google Sheets and press <kbd class="mod-key">Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>V</kbd> anywhere on this page, or drop a CSV or Excel file here.</p>
        <p class="drop-links"><button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="pasteBtn" hidden>Paste</button><span aria-hidden="true" id="pasteSep" hidden>·</span><button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="pickFile">Choose a file</button><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="blankSheet">Start with an empty sheet</button><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="exampleBtn">Try an example</button><span aria-hidden="true" id="undoSep" hidden>·</span><button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="undoClear" hidden>Undo clear</button></p>
        <p class="jsal-error" id="dropError" role="alert" hidden></p>
        <div class="drop-desk" id="dropDesk" hidden>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="12" rx="2"/><path d="M8 20h8M12 16v4"/></svg>
          <p><b>Easiest on a computer.</b> Your sheet and the file sit side by side there.</p>
          <p><button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="shareBtn">Send this page to my computer</button></p>
        </div>
        <p class="drop-privacy">Everything stays in your browser. Nothing is uploaded.</p>
        <input type="file" id="fileInput" accept=".csv,.tsv,.txt,.xlsx,text/csv,text/tab-separated-values,application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet" hidden>
      </div>

      <!-- Phones show one pane at a time -->
      <div class="jsal-seg views" role="tablist" aria-label="Show" data-needs-content>
        <button type="button" role="tab" id="viewSheet" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="sheetPane">Your sheet</button>
        <button type="button" role="tab" id="viewFile" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="filePane" tabindex="-1">File</button>
      </div>

      <!-- The visitor's own rows, editable; the notes under each cell say what the file does with it -->
      <section class="pane sheet-pane" id="sheetPane" aria-labelledby="sheetH" data-needs-content>
        <div class="pane-head">
          <h2 class="pane-title" id="sheetH">Your sheet</h2>
          <span class="pane-meta" id="sheetMeta"></span>
          <div class="jsal-seg filter" id="filter" aria-label="Show rows">
            <button type="button" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All <span></span></button>
            <button type="button" data-filter="ready" aria-pressed="false">Ready <span></span></button>
            <button type="button" data-filter="check" aria-pressed="false">Check <span></span></button>
            <button type="button" data-filter="bad" aria-pressed="false">Needs you <span></span></button>
            <button type="button" data-filter="out" aria-pressed="false">Left out <span></span></button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cols" id="cols" hidden>
          <label>Old addresses <select class="field" id="colOld"></select></label>
          <label>New addresses <select class="field" id="colNew"></select></label>
          <!-- The pickers only say where the addresses are; the file's own columns are written by the tool -->
          <p class="cols-hint">Pick only where the addresses are: the file’s other columns are filled in for you.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- What was done to every row at once, and problems on several rows with a fix for all of them -->
        <div class="overview" id="overview" hidden></div>
        <div class="pane-body">
          <table class="sheet">
            <colgroup><col class="c-n"><col class="c-st"><col><col><col class="c-x"></colgroup>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">#</th><th scope="col"><span class="sr-only">State</span></th><th scope="col">Old address</th><th scope="col">New address</th><th scope="col"><span class="sr-only">Delete</span></th></tr></thead>
            <tbody id="rows"></tbody>
          </table>
          <p class="filter-empty" id="filterEmpty" hidden>No rows here.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pane-foot">
          <button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="addRow">Add a row</button>
          <button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="copySheet">Copy sheet</button>
          <button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="undoAll" hidden>Undo my edits</button>
          <button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="otherFile">Use another file</button>
          <!-- The sheet is kept in this browser until Clear, so a reload or a slip of Back loses nothing -->
          <span class="kept" id="kept" hidden><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Kept in this browser</span>
          <button type="button" class="jsal-btn link danger" id="clearBtn">Clear</button>
        </div>
        <p class="jsal-error" id="sheetError" role="alert" hidden></p>
      </section>

      <!-- The file as it will be downloaded; the header row is editable, and Settings holds the rest -->
      <section class="pane file-pane" id="filePane" aria-labelledby="fileName" data-needs-content>
        <div class="pane-head">
          <h2 class="pane-title mono file-name" id="fileName"><input class="name-in" id="nameIn" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" aria-label="File name" title="Rename the file"><span class="name-end" id="nameEnd"></span></h2>
          <div class="jsal-seg parts" id="parts" aria-label="Part" hidden></div>
          <div class="file-acts">
            <button type="button" class="jsal-btn small set-btn" id="fmtBtn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="fmt"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M19.4 15a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33 1.82l.06.06a2 2 0 1 1-2.83 2.83l-.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82-.33 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1 1.51V21a2 2 0 1 1-4 0v-.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1-1.51 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82.33l-.06.06a2 2 0 1 1-2.83-2.83l.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33-1.82 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51-1H3a2 2 0 1 1 0-4h.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.51-1 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33-1.82l-.06-.06a2 2 0 1 1 2.83-2.83l.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82.33h0a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1-1.51V3a2 2 0 1 1 4 0v.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1 1.51 1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82-.33l.06-.06a2 2 0 1 1 2.83 2.83l-.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33 1.82v0a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.51 1H21a2 2 0 1 1 0 4h-.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51 1z"/></svg>Settings<svg class="chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="12" height="12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
            <button type="button" class="fmt-btn fold-btn" id="foldBtn" aria-label="Hide file">Hide<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="12" height="12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg></button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <!-- With the file hidden, the pane folds to a tab that says what's in the file, and the sheet takes the width -->
        <button type="button" class="fold-tab" id="unfoldBtn">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 6-6 6 6 6"/></svg>
          <svg class="fold-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><path d="M14 3v5h5M9 13h6M9 17h6"/></svg>
          <span class="fold-lbl">Show file</span>
          <span class="fold-num" id="foldCount"></span>
          <span id="foldRows"></span>
          <span class="fold-bad" id="foldBad" hidden></span>
        </button>
        <div class="fmt" id="fmt" hidden>
          <div class="opt" id="optNew"><span>New addresses</span><span class="jsal-seg"><button type="button" data-new="path" aria-pressed="true">Paths</button><button type="button" data-new="url" aria-pressed="false">Full URLs</button></span></div>
          <label class="opt" id="optSite" hidden><span>New site</span><input class="txt" id="newSite" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" placeholder="https://www.example.com"></label>
          <div class="opt" id="optCode"><span>Status</span><span class="jsal-seg" id="codeSeg"><button type="button" data-code="" aria-pressed="false">None</button><button type="button" data-code="301" aria-pressed="true">301</button><button type="button" data-code="302" aria-pressed="false">302</button></span></div>
          <label class="opt" id="optSep"><span>Separator</span><input class="txt short" id="sep" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" title="Type \t for a tab"></label>
          <p class="opt-foot"><button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="resetFmt" hidden>Back to the platform’s settings</button></p>
        </div>
        <!-- Rows that need fixing aren't in the file, said first so a partial file is never a surprise -->
        <p class="file-missing" id="fileMissing" hidden></p>
        <p class="file-done" id="fileDone" hidden><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg><span id="fileDoneText"></span></p>
        <!-- What could go wrong on this platform's import (a warning), then what's worth knowing -->
        <p class="file-box warn" id="fileWarn" hidden></p>
        <p class="file-box info" id="fileInfo" hidden></p>
        <div class="pane-body file-body">
          <!-- The header row is labelled where it sits, so whether the file has one is seen in the file itself; a long
               one wraps like the lines under it -->
          <div class="head-row" id="headRow">
            <div class="head-label">
              <span class="head-tag" aria-hidden="true">Header row</span>
              <button type="button" class="del head-del" id="headDel" aria-label="Remove the header row"><span aria-hidden="true">×</span></button>
            </div>
            <textarea class="head-in" id="headIn" rows="1" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Header row" aria-describedby="headWarn" title="Edit the header row"></textarea>
          </div>
          <p class="head-add" id="headAdd" hidden><span id="headAddText"></span> <button type="button" class="jsal-btn link" id="headAddBtn">Add one</button></p>
          <p class="head-warn" id="headWarn" hidden></p>
          <pre class="file" id="fileText" tabindex="0" aria-label="File contents"></pre>
          <p class="file-empty" id="fileEmpty" hidden>No redirects ready yet.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Fragment set:html={`<!-- About: below the app (which fills the first screen); styles in /shell.css -->`} />
  <section class="jsal-about" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-h">
    <h2 id="about-h">About Redirect Import</h2>
    <p class="jsal-lead">Turns a sheet of old and new addresses into the exact file your platform imports, and catches what would break the import before you upload it.</p>

    <h3>How to use it</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Copy the two columns from Excel or Google Sheets<span data-touch=" and tap Paste, or choose a CSV or Excel file.">, and press <kbd class="mod-key">Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>V</kbd> anywhere on the page, or drop a CSV or Excel file on it.</span></li>
      <li>Pick where you’re importing them.</li>
      <li>Fix anything marked red in your sheet. The file beside it changes as you type.</li>
      <li>Download the file, or copy it, and import it on the platform.</li>
    </ol>

    <details>
      <summary><h3>Getting a clean sheet</h3></summary>
      <ul>
        <li>Search Console exports at most 1,000 addresses for each issue in its Pages report, so on a bigger site add the old sitemap or a crawl to its list of pages not found.</li>
        <li>From Excel, save as CSV UTF-8. A plain CSV saves letters outside your computer’s language settings as ?, and a UTF-8 CSV opened with a double-click shows é as Ã©.</li>
      </ul>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary><h3>What it fixes for you</h3></summary>
      <ul>
        <li>Removes the domain from old addresses, and from new ones on your own site (addresses on other sites keep theirs).</li>
        <li>Removes tracking tags (utm_ and similar) and the # part from old addresses.</li>
        <li>Writes accented letters the way browsers send them (é becomes %C3%A9).</li>
        <li>Leaves out rows that point to themselves, repeat another row, or are marked “disregard”, “skip”, “delete”, “404” and the like instead of a new address.</li>
        <li>Splits columns pasted with spaces between them, as from an email or PDF.</li>
      </ul>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary><h3>What it asks you to fix</h3></summary>
      <ul>
        <li>Addresses cut short with …, as reports show long ones (copying the text copies the shortened address).</li>
        <li>New addresses on a preview or staging site (myshopify.com, webflow.io, wixsite.com, a staging subdomain, localhost and others), which would send visitors there once the site is live.</li>
        <li>Spaces, Word’s long dashes and curly quotes, hidden tabs and line breaks, a stray %, and characters an address can’t hold (&lt; &gt; " {"{"} {"}"} | \ ^ `).</li>
        <li>What audits and crawls copy in with the addresses: a full stop or bracket from the sentence around one, an address encoded twice (%2520 for a space), and letters garbled (é as Ã©) or saved as ?.</li>
        <li>Files, feeds, sitemaps and WordPress system addresses (/wp-admin, /wp-json) sent to a page, and one page listed several times with different ? parts (?page=2, ?sort=price) but never on its own.</li>
        <li>A missing old or new address.</li>
        <li>The same old address sent to two different places (you pick which row to keep), and loops.</li>
        <li>Addresses that differ only by the last / or capitals (/about-us/ and /About-us), which some platforms treat as one. They go in the file, marked to test after importing, except where a row would loop.</li>
        <li>Redirect chains, where one row moves A to B and another moves B to C. They go in the file as you typed them, marked to check, with a button that points A straight to C.</li>
        <li>Each platform’s own rules, from its help pages: addresses Shopify keeps for itself (/cart, /shop, /apps and others), no ? in old addresses on Squarespace and Duda, no % on Duda, up to 140 characters on HubSpot, and files split into parts where an import has a cap (500 for Wix and HubSpot, 200 for Duda).</li>
      </ul>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary><h3>Where it can import</h3></summary>
      <ul>
        <li>Shopify, Wix, Webflow, Framer (with its Redirect Sync plugin), HubSpot, BigCommerce and Duda: a CSV file.</li>
        <li>Squarespace: lines to paste into URL mappings. Ghost: a redirects.yaml file.</li>
        <li>WordPress: a CSV for the Redirection plugin, Rank Math (Pro) or Yoast SEO Premium.</li>
        <li>Netlify (_redirects), Vercel (vercel.json, or a bulk redirects CSV), Apache (.htaccess) and Nginx.</li>
        <li>Anything not listed: a plain CSV, with any header row and separator. Until you pick a platform, the file is this plain CSV.</li>
      </ul>
    </details>

    <h3>Common questions</h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>Can I change the header row or separator?</dt>
      <dd><span data-touch="Tap">Click</span> the header line in the file and type. The separator follows what you type, and Settings has the status column, full URLs and the rest.</dd>
      <dt>Why is my file in parts?</dt>
      <dd>Some platforms take a set number of redirects per import. Import each part in turn.</dd>
      <dt>Is my sheet uploaded anywhere?</dt>
      <dd>No. It’s read and checked in your browser, and kept there until you press Clear, so a reload doesn’t lose your edits.</dd>
    </dl>

    <p class="jsal-feedback">Useful? Ideas or problems? <a href="mailto:dev@jsal.io?subject=Redirect%20Import">Email me</a>.</p>
    <p><svg class="jsal-mark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect class="jsal-mark-tile" x=".5" y=".5" width="31" height="31" rx="6.5"/><path class="jsal-mark-j" d="M20 15V20a4.5 4.5 0 0 1-9 0"/><path class="jsal-mark-gem" d="M20 5l3 3-3 3-3-3z"/></svg>Made by <a href="/">John Salvador</a>. Also try the <a href="/cms-picker/">CMS Picker</a> to compare what each CMS can do, or <a href="/formatter/">Clean Paste</a> for clean HTML from Word and Google Docs. <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Page>
